IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc10-records.l4 -- sections 278.32 to 278.98 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: the end of the regime for records in the
-- accused's possession (publication bans, the jury instruction, appeals, the joint application, the repealed sections 278.4 to 278.97) and the
-- duty to give reasons in proceedings for sexual offences. Layer 1 (the law, objectively); the seat layer is ccc10-seat.l4.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE (the case is within the rule on the text's own words); JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words, quoted in
-- the branch's comment); NOTHING (not covered: the text is silent, limits a grant or prohibition in its own wording, or points outside the text).
-- A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE. Seams: `s 278.3 ...` is ccc9's answer (PLAN.md section 6); `s 2 complainant: ...` is the keel's `s 2 complainant`;
-- `s 787(1) ...` is ccc29's answer; both are taken as inputs of the types the answering functions give.

§ `s 278.32 -- Publication prohibited`

-- 278.32(1): who shall not publish what. The paragraphs name four kinds of matter about an application under 278.3(1).
-- src:5570 | 278.32 (1) A person shall not publish in any document, or broadcast or transmit in any way, any of the following:
-- src:5571 | (a) the contents of an application made under subsection 278.3(1);
-- src:5572 | (b) any evidence taken, the information given or the representations made at the consideration of an application made under subsection 278.3(1) or at a hearing under section 278.31;
-- src:5573 | (c) the decision of a judge, provincial court judge or justice under subsection 278.3(5), unless the judge, provincial court judge or justice, after taking into account the complainant’s right of privacy and the interests of justice, orders that the decision may be published, broadcast or transmitted;
-- src:5574 | (d) the determination made and the reasons provided under subsection 278.31(4), unless that determination is that evidence is admissible or the judge, provincial court judge or justice, after taking into account the complainant’s right of privacy and the interests of justice, orders that the determination and the reasons may be published, broadcast or transmitted.
@ref s 278.32(1) (src:5570-5574)
DECLARE `s 278.32(1) the matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 278.32(1)(a) the contents of an application`
    `s 278.32(1)(b) evidence taken, information given or representations made at the consideration of an application or at a hearing`
    `s 278.32(1)(c) the decision of a judge, provincial court judge or justice under subsection 278.3(5)`
    `s 278.32(1)(d) the determination made and the reasons provided under subsection 278.31(4)`
    `s 278.32(1) a matter that is none of (a) to (d)`

@ref s 278.32(1) (src:5570-5574)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 278.32(1) the matter`
      `s 278.3 an application for a hearing on records in the accused’s possession has been made` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the judge, provincial court judge or justice has ordered that it may be published, broadcast or transmitted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the determination is that evidence is admissible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.32(1) publication of the matter is prohibited` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 278.3 an application for a hearing on records in the accused’s possession has been made` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an application made under subsection 278.3(1)" (no such application is shown, or section 278.3's own answer is not covered)
    ELSE
        CONSIDER matter
        WHEN `s 278.32(1)(a) the contents of an application` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 278.32(1)(b) evidence taken, information given or representations made at the consideration of an application or at a hearing` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 278.32(1)(c) the decision of a judge, provincial court judge or justice under subsection 278.3(5)` THEN
            IF `the judge, provincial court judge or justice has ordered that it may be published, broadcast or transmitted`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the judge, provincial court judge or justice, after taking into account the complainant’s right of privacy and the interests of justice, orders that the decision may be published, broadcast or transmitted"
            ELSE JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 278.32(1)(d) the determination made and the reasons provided under subsection 278.31(4)` THEN
            IF `the determination is that evidence is admissible` OR `the judge, provincial court judge or justice has ordered that it may be published, broadcast or transmitted`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless that determination is that evidence is admissible or the judge, provincial court judge or justice"
            ELSE JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 278.32(1) a matter that is none of (a) to (d)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any of the following"

-- The regulative twin of 278.32(1): the prohibition on "a person" (the core's Party has no "any person", NEEDS-CORE.md).
-- The (c) and (d) carve-outs and subsection (1.1) are in the decision functions; the trace states the base prohibition.
DECLARE `s 278.32(1) the bearer of the prohibition` IS ONE OF `s 278.32(1) any person`
DECLARE `s 278.32(1) the prohibited act` IS ONE OF `s 278.32(1) publish, broadcast or transmit the matter`

@ref s 278.32(1) (src:5570)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 278.32(1) the bearer of the prohibition` `s 278.32(1) the prohibited act`
`s 278.32(1) the prohibition on publishing` MEANS
    PARTY `s 278.32(1) any person`
    SHANT `s 278.32(1) publish, broadcast or transmit the matter`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 278.32(1) any person` BECAUSE "published, broadcast or transmitted a matter that section 278.32(1) prohibits"

-- 278.32(1.1): the exception. "does not apply if": a flat negative; none of (a) to (c) holding is a failed "if" (marginal reading (a)).
-- src:5575 | Exception
-- src:5576 | (1.1) Subsection (1) does not apply if the disclosure of any information referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) to (d) is
-- src:5577 | (a) made in the course of the administration of justice when the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known in the community;
-- src:5578 | (b) made by the complainant or any witness and about that complainant or witness and their particulars, in any forum and for any purpose, and they did not intentionally or recklessly reveal the identity of or reveal particulars likely to identify any other person whose identity is protected by this section; or
-- src:5579 | (c) made by the complainant or any witness when the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known to the public, including when the disclosure is made to a legal professional, a health care professional or a person in a relationship of trust with the complainant or the witness.
@ref s 278.32(1.1) (src:5575-5579)
GIVEN `s 2 complainant: the person who made the disclosure is the complainant` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person who made the disclosure is a witness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.32(1.1) the disclosure is made by the complainant or any witness` MEANS
    IF (`s 2 complainant: the person who made the disclosure is the complainant` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the person who made the disclosure is a witness`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `s 2 complainant: the person who made the disclosure is the complainant` EQUALS NOTHING
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is the complainant is for s 2 "complainant" and is not determined
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "made by the complainant or any witness" (neither the complainant nor a witness)

@ref s 278.32(1.1) (src:5575-5579)
GIVEN `the information is referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made in the course of the administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known in the community` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 278.32(1.1) as to who made the disclosure` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is about that complainant or witness and their particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they did not intentionally or recklessly reveal the identity of or particulars likely to identify any other person whose identity is protected by this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.32(1.1) subsection (1) does not apply to the disclosure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the information is referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) to (d)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the disclosure of any information referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) to (d)"
        IF `limb (a)` OR (`limb (b) apart from who made the disclosure` AND (`the answer of s 278.32(1.1) as to who made the disclosure` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) OR (`limb (c) apart from who made the disclosure` AND (`the answer of s 278.32(1.1) as to who made the disclosure` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the answer of s 278.32(1.1) as to who made the disclosure` EQUALS NOTHING) AND (`limb (b) apart from who made the disclosure` OR `limb (c) apart from who made the disclosure`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): who made the disclosure turns on s 2 "complainant", which is not determined
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply if the disclosure" (none of (a) to (c) holds: a failed "if", marginal reading (a))
    WHERE
        `limb (a)` MEANS `the disclosure is made in the course of the administration of justice` AND `the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known in the community`
        `limb (b) apart from who made the disclosure` MEANS `the disclosure is about that complainant or witness and their particulars` AND `they did not intentionally or recklessly reveal the identity of or particulars likely to identify any other person whose identity is protected by this section`
        `limb (c) apart from who made the disclosure` MEANS `the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known to the public`

-- 278.32(2): the offence. Every person who contravenes (1): the published matter, (1) answering JUST TRUE, and (1.1) not excusing it.
-- src:5580 | Offence
-- src:5581 | (2) Every person who contravenes subsection (1) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 278.32(2) (src:5580-5581)
GIVEN `the person published, broadcast or transmitted the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 278.32(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 278.32(1.1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.32(2) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person published, broadcast or transmitted the matter` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who contravenes subsection (1)" (the section is silent about a person who did not publish)
        IF (`the answer of s 278.32(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the answer of s 278.32(1.1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the answer of s 278.32(1.1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the answer of s 278.32(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply if the disclosure" (an exception that applies) or "unless the judge, provincial court judge or justice" (an order lifting the bar): no contravention of subsection (1), so no offence under this subsection
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of subsection (1) or (1.1) is not covered

@ref s 278.32(2) (src:5580-5581)
`s 278.32(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 278.32(2) (src:5580-5581)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 278.32(2) the punishment` MEANS `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

§ `s 278.33 -- Instruction to jury: use of evidence`

-- src:5583 | 278.33 If evidence is admitted at trial on the basis of a determination made under subsection 278.31(4), the judge shall instruct the jury as to the uses that the jury may and may not make of that evidence.
@ref s 278.33 (src:5583)
GIVEN `evidence is admitted at trial on the basis of a determination made under subsection 278.31(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.33 the judge shall instruct the jury as to the uses that the jury may and may not make of the evidence` MEANS
    IF `evidence is admitted at trial on the basis of a determination made under subsection 278.31(4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If evidence is admitted at trial on the basis of a determination made under subsection 278.31(4)" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))

DECLARE `s 278.33 the act of the judge` IS ONE OF `s 278.33 instruct the jury as to the uses that the jury may and may not make of that evidence`

@ref s 278.33 (src:5583)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 278.33 the act of the judge`
`s 278.33 the duty to instruct the jury` MEANS
    PARTY `a judge`
    MUST `s 278.33 instruct the jury as to the uses that the jury may and may not make of that evidence`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a judge` BECAUSE "the jury was not instructed as to the uses it may and may not make of the evidence"

§ `s 278.34 -- Appeal`

-- src:5585 | 278.34 For the purposes of sections 675 and 676, a determination made under subsection 278.31(4) is deemed to be a question of law.
@ref s 278.34 (src:5585)
GIVEN `the determination is one made under subsection 278.31(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose, as the section of the Code for whose purposes the question is asked` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.34 the determination is deemed to be a question of law` MEANS
    IF `the determination is one made under subsection 278.31(4)` AND (`the purpose, as the section of the Code for whose purposes the question is asked`'s `section` EQUALS 675 OR `the purpose, as the section of the Code for whose purposes the question is asked`'s `section` EQUALS 676)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of sections 675 and 676, a determination made under subsection 278.31(4)"

§ `s 278.35 -- Joint application`

-- 278.35(1): the joint application. "may jointly apply" is a grant: a failed gate gives NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-12), one fork line in NOTES.md.
-- src:5587 | Joint Application
-- src:5588 | Admissibility of record
-- src:5589 | 278.35 (1) The prosecutor and the accused, together with the complainant or any witness to which a record, or part of it, relates, may jointly apply to the judge before whom the accused is to be, or is being, tried for a determination as to whether the record, or any part of it, is admissible under subsection 278.29(2) without holding a hearing under section 278.31.
@ref s 278.35(1) (src:5587-5589)
GIVEN `the applicants are the prosecutor and the accused, together with the complainant or any witness to which the record or part relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made to the judge before whom the accused is to be, or is being, tried` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is for a determination whether the record or part is admissible under subsection 278.29(2) without holding a hearing under section 278.31` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.35(1) the applicants may jointly apply for a determination without a hearing` MEANS
    IF `the applicants are the prosecutor and the accused, together with the complainant or any witness to which the record or part relates`
       AND `the application is made to the judge before whom the accused is to be, or is being, tried`
       AND `the application is for a determination whether the record or part is admissible under subsection 278.29(2) without holding a hearing under section 278.31`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The prosecutor and the accused, together with the complainant or any witness to which a record, or part of it, relates, may jointly apply to the judge before whom the accused is to be, or is being, tried"

-- 278.35(2): form and content. "must" not met is JUST FALSE (a fork line: a bare "must" not done).
-- src:5590 | Form and content
-- src:5591 | (2) The application must be made in writing and signed by the applicants and must set out the detailed particulars of the record or part and
-- src:5592 | (a) the relevance of that record or part to an issue at trial;
-- src:5593 | (b) if the admissibility of the record or part is subject to section 276, how it meets the conditions set out in subsection 276(2) while taking into account the factors set out in subsection 278.29(3);
-- src:5594 | (c) that the record or part has significant probative value that is not substantially outweighed by the danger of prejudice to the proper administration of justice; and
-- src:5595 | (d) any information the applicants consider necessary to assist the judge when the judge takes into account the factors referred to in subsection 278.29(3).
@ref s 278.35(2) (src:5590-5595)
GIVEN `the application is made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is signed by the applicants` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application sets out the detailed particulars of the record or part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out the relevance of that record or part to an issue at trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the admissibility of the record or part is subject to section 276` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out how the record or part meets the conditions set out in subsection 276(2) while taking into account the factors set out in subsection 278.29(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out that the record or part has significant probative value that is not substantially outweighed by the danger of prejudice to the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out any information the applicants consider necessary to assist the judge when the judge takes into account the factors referred to in subsection 278.29(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.35(2) the application meets the form and content required` MEANS
    IF     `the application is made in writing`
       AND `the application is signed by the applicants`
       AND `the application sets out the detailed particulars of the record or part`
       AND `it sets out the relevance of that record or part to an issue at trial`
       AND ((NOT `the admissibility of the record or part is subject to section 276`) OR `it sets out how the record or part meets the conditions set out in subsection 276(2) while taking into account the factors set out in subsection 278.29(3)`)
       AND `it sets out that the record or part has significant probative value that is not substantially outweighed by the danger of prejudice to the proper administration of justice`
       AND `it sets out any information the applicants consider necessary to assist the judge when the judge takes into account the factors referred to in subsection 278.29(3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application must be made in writing and signed by the applicants and must set out the detailed particulars of the record or part" (a bare "must" not met)

-- 278.35(3): a copy filed with the clerk of the court "at least 60 days before the trial". Days between the two dates, counted as calendar days.
-- src:5596 | Copy to clerk
-- src:5597 | (3) A copy of the application must be filed with the clerk of the court at least 60 days before the trial.
@ref s 278.35(3) (src:5596-5597)
GIVEN `the day on which the copy was filed with the clerk of the court` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the trial begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.35(3) the copy of the application was filed with the clerk of the court at least 60 days before the trial` MEANS
    IF (DATE_SERIAL `the day on which the trial begins`) MINUS (DATE_SERIAL `the day on which the copy was filed with the clerk of the court`) AT LEAST 60
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be filed with the clerk of the court at least 60 days before the trial" (a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))

-- 278.35(4): the judge "shall" consider and determine "no later than 30 days after the day on which the application is made".
-- src:5598 | Determination and reasons
-- src:5599 | (4) The judge, provincial court judge or justice shall, in the absence of the applicants, and without holding a hearing, consider the application and make a determination no later than 30 days after the day on which the application is made as to whether the evidence, or part of it, is admissible under subsection 278.29(2) and shall provide reasons for that determination, and
-- src:5600 | (a) if not all of the evidence is to be admitted, the reasons must state the part of the evidence that is to be admitted;
-- src:5601 | (b) the reasons must state the factors referred to in subsection 276(3) or 278.29(3) that affected the determination; and
-- src:5602 | (c) if all or any part of the evidence is to be admitted, the reasons must state the manner in which that evidence is expected to be relevant to an issue at trial.
@ref s 278.35(4) (src:5598-5602)
GIVEN `the day on which the application is made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the determination is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.35(4) the determination was made no later than 30 days after the day on which the application was made` MEANS
    IF (DATE_SERIAL `the day on which the determination is made`) MINUS (DATE_SERIAL `the day on which the application is made`) AT MOST 30
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "make a determination no later than 30 days after the day on which the application is made" (a period the text fixes in its own words)

@ref s 278.35(4)(a) to (c) (src:5599-5602)
GIVEN `not all of the evidence is to be admitted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reasons state the part of the evidence that is to be admitted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reasons state the factors referred to in subsection 276(3) or 278.29(3) that affected the determination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all or any part of the evidence is to be admitted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reasons state the manner in which that evidence is expected to be relevant to an issue at trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.35(4) the reasons state what paragraphs (a) to (c) require` MEANS
    IF     ((NOT `not all of the evidence is to be admitted`) OR `the reasons state the part of the evidence that is to be admitted`)
       AND `the reasons state the factors referred to in subsection 276(3) or 278.29(3) that affected the determination`
       AND ((NOT `all or any part of the evidence is to be admitted`) OR `the reasons state the manner in which that evidence is expected to be relevant to an issue at trial`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the reasons must state" (a bare "must" not met, in limb (a), (b) or (c))

DECLARE `s 278.35(4) the act of the judge` IS ONE OF `s 278.35(4) consider the application and make a determination, with reasons`

@ref s 278.35(4) (src:5598-5599)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 278.35(4) the act of the judge`
`s 278.35(4) the duty to determine the application within 30 days` MEANS
    PARTY `a judge`
    MUST `s 278.35(4) consider the application and make a determination, with reasons`
    WITHIN 30   -- days, counted from the day on which the application is made (the trace starts at that day, AT 0)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a judge` BECAUSE "no determination was made within 30 days after the day on which the application was made"

-- 278.35(5): the two sentences, one function each. "If ... satisfied ... shall grant"; "If ... not so satisfied ... shall hold a hearing".
-- src:5603 | Power to grant application or hold hearing
-- src:5604 | (5) If the judge, provincial court judge or justice is satisfied that the record, or part of it, is admissible under subsection 278.29(2), the judge, provincial court judge or justice shall grant the application. If the judge, provincial court judge or justice is not so satisfied, they shall hold a hearing under section 278.31 to determine whether the evidence is admissible under subsection 278.29(2).
@ref s 278.35(5) (src:5603-5604)
GIVEN `the judge, provincial court judge or justice is satisfied that the record, or part of it, is admissible under subsection 278.29(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.35(5) the judge shall grant the application` MEANS
    IF `the judge, provincial court judge or justice is satisfied that the record, or part of it, is admissible under subsection 278.29(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the judge, provincial court judge or justice is satisfied that the record, or part of it, is admissible under subsection 278.29(2), the judge, provincial court judge or justice shall grant the application" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))

@ref s 278.35(5) (src:5603-5604)
GIVEN `the judge, provincial court judge or justice is satisfied that the record, or part of it, is admissible under subsection 278.29(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.35(5) the judge shall hold a hearing under section 278.31` MEANS
    IF NOT `the judge, provincial court judge or justice is satisfied that the record, or part of it, is admissible under subsection 278.29(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the judge, provincial court judge or justice is not so satisfied, they shall hold a hearing under section 278.31" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))

DECLARE `s 278.35(5) the act of the judge` IS ONE OF
    `s 278.35(5) grant the application`
    `s 278.35(5) hold a hearing under section 278.31`

@ref s 278.35(5) (src:5603-5604)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that the record, or part of it, is admissible under subsection 278.29(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 278.35(5) the act of the judge`
`s 278.35(5) the duty to grant the application or hold a hearing` MEANS
    IF `the judge is satisfied that the record, or part of it, is admissible under subsection 278.29(2)`
    THEN PARTY `a judge` MUST `s 278.35(5) grant the application` HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY `a judge` BECAUSE "the judge was satisfied that the record is admissible and did not grant the application"
    ELSE PARTY `a judge` MUST `s 278.35(5) hold a hearing under section 278.31` HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY `a judge` BECAUSE "the judge was not so satisfied and did not hold a hearing under section 278.31"

