    IF `the record is a therapeutic record`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "this section does not apply to a therapeutic record"

-- src:5609 | For greater certainty — right to counsel
-- src:5610 | (8) For greater certainty, the complainant or any witness has the right to be represented by counsel.
@ref s 278.35(8) (src:5609-5610)
GIVEN `s 2 complainant: the person is the complainant` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a witness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.35(8) the person has the right to be represented by counsel` MEANS
    IF (`s 2 complainant: the person is the complainant` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the person is a witness`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the complainant or any witness has the right to be represented by counsel" (a right stated for the complainant and witnesses; the section is silent about anyone else)

§ `s 278.36 -- Publication prohibited (joint application)`

-- src:5612 | 278.36 (1) A person shall not publish in any document, or broadcast or transmit in any way, any of the following:
-- src:5613 | (a) the contents of an application made under subsection 278.35(1);
-- src:5614 | (b) any evidence taken, the information given or the representations made at the consideration of an application made under subsection 278.35(1);
-- src:5615 | (c) the determination made and the reasons provided under section 278.35, unless that determination is that the record or part of it is admissible or the judge, provincial court judge or justice, after taking into account the complainant’s right of privacy and the interests of justice, orders that the determination and the reasons may be published, broadcast or transmitted.
@ref s 278.36(1) (src:5612-5615)
DECLARE `s 278.36(1) the matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 278.36(1)(a) the contents of an application`
    `s 278.36(1)(b) evidence taken, information given or representations made at the consideration of an application`
    `s 278.36(1)(c) the determination made and the reasons provided under section 278.35`
    `s 278.36(1) a matter that is none of (a) to (c)`

@ref s 278.36(1) (src:5612-5615)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 278.36(1) the matter`
      `an application under subsection 278.35(1) has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the determination is that the record or part of it is admissible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge, provincial court judge or justice has ordered that it may be published, broadcast or transmitted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.36(1) publication of the matter is prohibited` MEANS
    IF NOT `an application under subsection 278.35(1) has been made`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an application made under subsection 278.35(1)"
    ELSE
        CONSIDER matter
        WHEN `s 278.36(1)(a) the contents of an application` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 278.36(1)(b) evidence taken, information given or representations made at the consideration of an application` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 278.36(1)(c) the determination made and the reasons provided under section 278.35` THEN
            IF `the determination is that the record or part of it is admissible` OR `the judge, provincial court judge or justice has ordered that it may be published, broadcast or transmitted`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless that determination is that the record or part of it is admissible or the judge, provincial court judge or justice"
            ELSE JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 278.36(1) a matter that is none of (a) to (c)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any of the following"

DECLARE `s 278.36(1) the bearer of the prohibition` IS ONE OF `s 278.36(1) any person`
DECLARE `s 278.36(1) the prohibited act` IS ONE OF `s 278.36(1) publish, broadcast or transmit the matter`

@ref s 278.36(1) (src:5612)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 278.36(1) the bearer of the prohibition` `s 278.36(1) the prohibited act`
`s 278.36(1) the prohibition on publishing` MEANS
    PARTY `s 278.36(1) any person`
    SHANT `s 278.36(1) publish, broadcast or transmit the matter`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 278.36(1) any person` BECAUSE "published, broadcast or transmitted a matter that section 278.36(1) prohibits"

-- src:5616 | Exception
-- src:5617 | (1.1) Subsection (1) does not apply if the disclosure of any information referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) to (c) is
-- src:5618 | (a) made in the course of the administration of justice when the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known in the community;
-- src:5619 | (b) made by the complainant or any witness and about that complainant or witness and their particulars, in any forum and for any purpose, and they did not intentionally or recklessly reveal the identity of or reveal particulars likely to identify any other person whose identity is protected by this section; or
-- src:5620 | (c) made by the complainant or any witness when the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known to the public, including when the disclosure is made to a legal professional, a health care professional or a person in a relationship of trust with the complainant or the witness.
@ref s 278.36(1.1) (src:5616-5620)
GIVEN `s 2 complainant: the person who made the disclosure is the complainant` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person who made the disclosure is a witness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.36(1.1) the disclosure is made by the complainant or any witness` MEANS
    IF (`s 2 complainant: the person who made the disclosure is the complainant` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the person who made the disclosure is a witness`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `s 2 complainant: the person who made the disclosure is the complainant` EQUALS NOTHING
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is the complainant is for s 2 "complainant" and is not determined
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "made by the complainant or any witness" (neither the complainant nor a witness)

@ref s 278.36(1.1) (src:5616-5620)
GIVEN `the information is referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) to (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made in the course of the administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known in the community` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 278.36(1.1) as to who made the disclosure` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is about that complainant or witness and their particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they did not intentionally or recklessly reveal the identity of or particulars likely to identify any other person whose identity is protected by this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.36(1.1) subsection (1) does not apply to the disclosure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the information is referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) to (c)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the disclosure of any information referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) to (c)"
        IF `limb (a)` OR (`limb (b) apart from who made the disclosure` AND (`the answer of s 278.36(1.1) as to who made the disclosure` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) OR (`limb (c) apart from who made the disclosure` AND (`the answer of s 278.36(1.1) as to who made the disclosure` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the answer of s 278.36(1.1) as to who made the disclosure` EQUALS NOTHING) AND (`limb (b) apart from who made the disclosure` OR `limb (c) apart from who made the disclosure`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): who made the disclosure turns on s 2 "complainant", which is not determined
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply if the disclosure" (none of (a) to (c) holds: a failed "if", marginal reading (a))
    WHERE
        `limb (a)` MEANS `the disclosure is made in the course of the administration of justice` AND `the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known in the community`
        `limb (b) apart from who made the disclosure` MEANS `the disclosure is about that complainant or witness and their particulars` AND `they did not intentionally or recklessly reveal the identity of or particulars likely to identify any other person whose identity is protected by this section`
        `limb (c) apart from who made the disclosure` MEANS `the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known to the public`

-- src:5621 | Offence
-- src:5622 | (2) Every person who contravenes subsection (1) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 278.36(2) (src:5621-5622)
GIVEN `the person published, broadcast or transmitted the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 278.36(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 278.36(1.1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.36(2) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person published, broadcast or transmitted the matter` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who contravenes subsection (1)" (the section is silent about a person who did not publish)
        IF (`the answer of s 278.36(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the answer of s 278.36(1.1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the answer of s 278.36(1.1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the answer of s 278.36(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply if the disclosure" (an exception that applies) or "unless the judge, provincial court judge or justice" (an order lifting the bar): no contravention of subsection (1), so no offence under this subsection
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of subsection (1) or (1.1) is not covered

@ref s 278.36(2) (src:5621-5622)
`s 278.36(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 278.36(2) (src:5621-5622)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 278.36(2) the punishment` MEANS `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:5624 | 278.37 If evidence is admitted at trial on the basis of a determination made under subsection 278.35(4), the judge shall instruct the jury as to the uses that the jury may and may not make of that evidence.
@ref s 278.37 (src:5624)
GIVEN `evidence is admitted at trial on the basis of a determination made under subsection 278.35(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.37 the judge shall instruct the jury as to the uses that the jury may and may not make of the evidence` MEANS
    IF `evidence is admitted at trial on the basis of a determination made under subsection 278.35(4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If evidence is admitted at trial on the basis of a determination made under subsection 278.35(4)" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))

DECLARE `s 278.37 the act of the judge` IS ONE OF `s 278.37 instruct the jury as to the uses that the jury may and may not make of that evidence`

@ref s 278.37 (src:5624)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 278.37 the act of the judge`
`s 278.37 the duty to instruct the jury` MEANS
    PARTY `a judge`
    MUST `s 278.37 instruct the jury as to the uses that the jury may and may not make of that evidence`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a judge` BECAUSE "the jury was not instructed as to the uses it may and may not make of the evidence"

-- src:5626 | 278.38 For the purposes of sections 675 and 676, a determination made under subsection 278.35(4) or (5) is deemed to be a question of law.
@ref s 278.38 (src:5626)
GIVEN `the determination is one made under subsection 278.35(4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose, as the section of the Code for whose purposes the question is asked` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.38 the determination is deemed to be a question of law` MEANS
    IF `the determination is one made under subsection 278.35(4) or (5)` AND (`the purpose, as the section of the Code for whose purposes the question is asked`'s `section` EQUALS 675 OR `the purpose, as the section of the Code for whose purposes the question is asked`'s `section` EQUALS 676)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of sections 675 and 676, a determination made under subsection 278.35(4) or (5)"

