§ `s 278.98 -- Reasons in certain proceedings`

-- 278.98(1): the offences are named by section number (seam rule R1), so the scope is tested against the core's `Provision of the Code`.
-- src:5643 | 278.98 (1) In proceedings in respect of an offence under section 151, 152, 153, 153.1 or 155, subsection 160(2) or (3) or section 170, 171, 172, 173, 271, 272 or 273, the judge shall provide reasons for a decision that a person is
@ref s 278.98(1) lead-in (src:5643)
GIVEN offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.98(1) the offence is one of those the subsection names` MEANS
    IF     offence's `section` EQUALS 151 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 152 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 153 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 153.1 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 155
        OR (offence's `section` EQUALS 160 AND (offence's `subsection` EQUALS "(2)" OR offence's `subsection` EQUALS "(3)"))
        OR offence's `section` EQUALS 170 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 171 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 172 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 173
        OR offence's `section` EQUALS 271 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 272 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 273
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In proceedings in respect of an offence under section 151, 152, 153, 153.1 or 155, subsection 160(2) or (3) or section 170, 171, 172, 173, 271, 272 or 273"

DECLARE `s 278.98(1) the decision` IS ONE OF
    `s 278.98(1)(a) acquitted`
    `s 278.98(1)(b) found guilty`
    `s 278.98(1)(c) discharged, after having been found guilty`
    `s 278.98(1)(d) found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder`
    `s 278.98(1)(e) found unfit to stand trial`
    `s 278.98(1) a decision of another kind`

-- src:5644 | (a) acquitted;
-- src:5645 | (b) found guilty;
-- src:5646 | (c) discharged, after having been found guilty;
-- src:5647 | (d) found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder; or
-- src:5648 | (e) found unfit to stand trial.
@ref s 278.98(1)(a) to (e) (src:5644-5648)
GIVEN decision IS A `s 278.98(1) the decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.98(1) the decision is one of those the subsection names` MEANS
    CONSIDER decision
    WHEN `s 278.98(1)(a) acquitted` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 278.98(1)(b) found guilty` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 278.98(1)(c) discharged, after having been found guilty` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 278.98(1)(d) found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 278.98(1)(e) found unfit to stand trial` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 278.98(1) a decision of another kind` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a decision that a person is"

DECLARE `s 278.98(1) the act of the judge` IS ONE OF `s 278.98(1) provide reasons for the decision`

@ref s 278.98(1) (src:5644-5648)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 278.98(1) the act of the judge`
`s 278.98(1) the duty to provide reasons` MEANS
    PARTY `a judge`
    MUST `s 278.98(1) provide reasons for the decision`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a judge` BECAUSE "no reasons were provided for the decision"

-- src:5649 | Historical offences
-- src:5650 | (2) Subsection (1) also applies in proceedings for any offence under this Act, as it read from time to time before the day on which this section comes into force, if the conduct alleged would be an offence referred to in subsection (1) if it occurred on or after that day.
@ref s 278.98(2) (src:5649-5650)
GIVEN `the proceedings are for an offence under this Act as it read from time to time before the day on which section 278.98 comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct alleged would be an offence referred to in subsection (1) if it occurred on or after that day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.98(2) subsection (1) also applies to the proceedings for the historical offence` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are for an offence under this Act as it read from time to time before the day on which section 278.98 comes into force` AND `the conduct alleged would be an offence referred to in subsection (1) if it occurred on or after that day`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) also applies in proceedings for any offence under this Act, as it read from time to time before the day on which this section comes into force, if the conduct alleged would be an offence" (the day itself is outside the sources)

-- src:5653 | Proceedings before judge
-- src:5654 | (4) This section applies only in proceedings before a judge without a jury.
@ref s 278.98(4) (src:5653-5654)
GIVEN `the proceedings are before a judge without a jury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.98(4) section 278.98 applies to the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are before a judge without a jury`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies only in proceedings before a judge without a jury"

-- The composition of (1), (2) and (4): the judge shall provide reasons. A "no" only from (4)'s "only"; otherwise NOTHING.
@ref s 278.98 composed from subsections (1), (2) and (4) (src:5653-5654)
GIVEN `the answer of s 278.98(1) as to the offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 278.98(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 278.98(1) as to the decision` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 278.98(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.98 the judge shall provide reasons for the decision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the answer of s 278.98(4)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies only in proceedings before a judge without a jury"
        IF ((`the answer of s 278.98(1) as to the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the answer of s 278.98(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) AND (`the answer of s 278.98(1) as to the decision` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the answer of s 278.98(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In proceedings in respect of an offence under section 151, 152, 153, 153.1 or 155" and "a decision that a person is" (an offence or a decision outside the lists, or an answer not covered)

DECLARE `s 278.98(3) how the reasons are given` IS ONE OF
    `s 278.98(3) the reasons are entered in the record of the proceedings`
    `s 278.98(3) the reasons are provided in writing`

-- src:5651 | Record of reasons
-- src:5652 | (3) The reasons shall be entered in the record of the proceedings or, if the proceedings are not recorded, shall be provided in writing.
@ref s 278.98(3) (src:5651-5652)
GIVEN `the proceedings are recorded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 278.98(3) how the reasons are given`
`s 278.98(3) the way the reasons are given` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are recorded`
    THEN `s 278.98(3) the reasons are entered in the record of the proceedings`
    ELSE `s 278.98(3) the reasons are provided in writing`
